    {
      "id": "claim_6a4d484b1c1f4dbea9f283df8c79cfb4",
      "statement": "The SPA is baked into the binary at compile time via `#[derive(RustEmbed)] #[folder = \"../web/dist/\"]`, so any frontend change requires rebuilding `web/dist` and recompiling the binary; the handler serves files from an embedded asset lookup with a hand-rolled MIME table and always answers 200, meaning a missing asset returns `index.html` as HTML.",
      "evidence": [
